WEBVTT

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.700
This is Hinomoto Girls Academy.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.440
A girls' boarding high school.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:13.000
The slightly strict rules make 
the students feel at ease.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.750
And the girls are raised like flowers 
in a well-maintained greenhouse,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.840
with a peaceful everyday life.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:31.880
And here in the greenhouse 
that is the Shinsen dorm,

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.800
beautiful flowers are in bloom.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.140
So hot...

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.100
Can't somebody do something 
about this heat?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:25.620
This glamorous and charming... girl... is?

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.920
This girl is Kondou Isami,

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.700
the head of this dorm, 
who is also known as the Golden Peony.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.170
So hot...

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.820
Kacchan, should you really 
be dressed like that?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.550
<b>The 

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.150
Does it really matter?

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:48.680
This cool and dangerous beauty 
is Hijikata Toshizou,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.560
the second in command of the dorms, known as the Black Bellflower.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:01.300
Um, Kondou-san and Hijikata-san...

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.720
Well...

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.470
And this girl with the dazzling 
eyes and elegant style...

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:11.970
who still somehow seems 
unlucky, is Okita Souji.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.830
She is also known as the White Lily.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:15.990
Though sickly and weak,

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.820
she's said to be the strongest 
of them all, however...

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:21.100
Kacchan, want an apple?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.930
Sure, thanks.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.800
What about you, Souji?

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.410
Um, I've been saying 
this for a while now.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:33.730
I'm sick with a cold today, 
so I can't talk with you.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.220
So why are you still here?

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.740
I don't understand why.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.240
Why?

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.990
Why, huh?

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:47.480
No reason, really.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.920
Right, Toshi?

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.620
Yup, none.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.450
Then why don't you go 
back to your own room...

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.790
Are you okay, Souji?

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.000
See?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.160
We're here because we're 
worried about you.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.010
That's right.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:07.390
Nobody wants to be alone 
when they're sick.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.160
You have a fever.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.770
Yeah, it's pretty hot.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.880
We'll have to cool you down.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.440
Yup, yup!

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.520
No, please don't worry about me.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.450
Actually, I'd prefer you left...

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.620
We'll cool you down.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.990
Toshi, get it nice and cold in here.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.640
Feels so good.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.900
It's so cool in here now.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.330
You cooled down the room?

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.200
Okita Souji, AKA the White Lily.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.970
Weak and sickly, but said to be 
the strongest of them all...

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:50.680
However, nobody has ever seen 
that for themselves.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.240
<b>The 

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.640
What are you gonna do with that?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.900
It's old, so I'm going 
to use it as a rag.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.610
You're always such a show off.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.760
Use a pair of scissors.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.790
That's no fun though.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.680
Should I not do it?

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.710
No, it's fun so it's fine.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:22.840
Anyway,

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.980
we just throw our clothes in 
this box and it does everything...

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.600
Everything's so convenient
in this world.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.600
Yeah.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.030
A lot of things surprised me 
since I came to this world.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.140
Appliances, is that what they call them?

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.800
Those surprise me the most.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:43.000
Yeah, it wasn't so much 
surprising as it was that they

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.360
got mad at us.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.950
<i>Good morning.</i>

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.950
<i>Is the bottom of the pot dirty?</i>

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.030
That scared the heck out of me.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:56.250
But you're used to them now, right?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:01.630
Um, 600 watts for three 
minutes and thirty seconds.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.210
Yeah. Very true.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.900
But I'm not as used to 
this world as you are.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.000
Really?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.800
When we came here...

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.350
It's obviously high school 
girls who run this world!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.440
So I shall live in this world 
as a high school girl!

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.110
I can pull it off! It'll be fine!

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.080
<i>No...</i>

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.700
<i>That's impossible.</i>

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:33.210
I seriously didn't expect it to work.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.260
Really?

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.250
You look pretty young, 
so I figured it'd be fine.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.500
<i>No, I meant you.</i>

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:47.860
But now, the three of us 
are here and we're making

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.560
our way in the world 
as high school girls.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:54.360
But, it all worked out in the end, right?

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.630
That's right.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:58.090
Eventually, it rubs off on you.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.990
Well, maybe not.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.880
But we're a part of this world now.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.020
Yup.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.320
This might not be a bad way to live.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.260
Yup.

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:13.750
What is it?

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:14.830
This...

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.600
Don't mix your whites and colors!

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.130
Whose is this?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.170
Mine.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.340
The color certainly rubbed off on it.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.800
What a nice bath.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.560
You haven't added
anything to the bathwater yet?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.240
Oh, sorry.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.180
What should we use today?

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.440
Hm, what do we have?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.230
Let me see.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.130
Let's see...

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:05.850
Kusatsu, Noboribetsu, Arima, 
Dougo, Beppu...

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:06.880
And...

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.890
Something called the "Famous Hot 
Springs of the World" series.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.170
The Swiss Schinznach hot springs.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.090
And the Innot Hot Springs in Australia.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.010
And... What country is this from?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.410
Something called the Shiny Hot Springs?

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.810
Then let's try that Shiny stuff.

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:27.300
So you put some hot 
springs powder in here.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.500
Yep.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.080
What is this color?

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.640
It looks like a puddle.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.780
And it stinks, too!

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.190
Is it sulfur?

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.480
I think it's something worse.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.330
Is it not dissolving properly?

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.830
<b>The 

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.460
Don't use your sword, Hijikata-san!

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.030
What's wrong?

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:54.280
Look! Look!

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:55.430
At what?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.930
See? It's all shiny!

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:00.690
You're right.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:04.050
Here, over here!

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.900
This is amazing.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.110
Is this because of the hot springs?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:14.590
They say good medicine tastes bitter.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.870
So maybe good bathwater smells bad?

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.450
Yeah.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.650
Stop touching my boobs!

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:35.000
But mine...

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.970
They don't bounce much, do they?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.230
<i>The heavy rain will continue 
late into the night.</i>

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.030
It's still raining...

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.610
<b>The Famous Blade Izuminokami Kanesada</b>

00:09:58.800 --> 00:09:59.620
Done.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.370
<b>Weak and Sickly</b>

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.920
Hey, knock it off!

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.370
Jeez.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.960
What is this?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:13.530
It won't come off?

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:15.260
This doesn't come off?!

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.040
Boring.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.800
It was just like stamping anything else.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.640
That joke didn't work too well, Toshi.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.900
Sorry. It wasn't funny at all.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.350
It wasn't, was it?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.570
It's a sign that your 
brain isn't working.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:32.570
It's lacking?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.190
Yeah. We need more sweets.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:38.990
What is it?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.000
No!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:48.040
I'm not running out in 
this rain to buy candy!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.240
I didn't mention it before,

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.960
but I've been running a fever all day.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:57.460
I was thinking of climbing into 
a warm bed and going to sleep.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.300
So you can go back to your rooms...

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.100
You should've kept your mouth shut.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:07.980
You predicted exactly what 
we were going to ask.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:12.500
No... I didn't do anything that special.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.180
You guys never think of 
anything that complex—

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.280
Look.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:21.150
Your warm futon is now my hostage.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:28.290
If you want it back, 
you'll have to fulfill our demands.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.420
Fine, fine.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.170
All right.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.950
Do whatever you want.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.300
Souji, let's play a game.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.720
A game?

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.130
Very well.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:49.470
I accept.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:53.710
I won't hold back, even against you.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.060
Prepare yourselves.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.450
<b>The 

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:09.630
You may not invade my territory.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.870
That's not part of the rules!

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:16.630
I'm so sorry I couldn't save you.

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:18.830
So, holding back, huh?

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.240
Did she?

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.390
Do you even know the rules to the game?

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:32.250
What the...

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.140
That's impossible.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.020
It's love power!

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:40.650
Fine, we'll fight with this.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:44.460
It's a simple game where you spin 
the roulette and move your piece.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:49.290
You pull a card each turn 
and do whatever it says.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:52.960
The person with the most 
money at the goal wins.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:55.750
Life's about more than money, though.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.250
Indeed.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.140
Here I go!

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:05.070
Your autobiography sells like hotcakes.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.680
You buy land with the proceeds.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.980
The value of the land goes up 
and you make even more money.

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:21.280
The stock of the company you invested 
in rises and you're all smiles!

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.240
If I get a three, I win.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.850
And right now, I have the most money.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.090
Even if I get an awful card,

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:33.860
it probably won't depress me too much.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:38.290
Both of you, behold my beautiful life!

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:42.960
Love power.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:46.950
Yay!

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.460
I did it.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.580
Your happiness as you win

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.370
your favorite game lasts 
only for a moment.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.860
You have to go to the
convenience store in the rain to buy

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:02.580
candy for your beloved upperclassmen.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.950
Congratulations on your victory.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.480
Hey, you have to do whatever 
it says on the card, right?

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.180
When was this card put in there?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.040
You thought of it as only a game.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:17.960
Souji,

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:22.170
to us, even a game is something 
you bet your life on.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:24.820
Do whatever you must to win.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:27.190
That is the true game of life!

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:28.590
Remember that.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.300
That sounds nice and all, 
but, basically, you just cheated.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.340
But, fine.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:36.540
I'll be back.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.940
Huh? The rain stopped.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:42.550
Then want to all go together?

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:43.850
Yeah.

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:46.620
It was supposed to pour all day.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.100
Is that love power, too?

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:53.640
But I left my wallet in my room.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.090
So did I.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.420
What?

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.180
Fine!

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:02.520
I'll pay.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.920
But pay me back, okay? Jeez!

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.040
We bought a lot of stuff.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:16.980
A lot of stuff.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.850
All the stuff.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:26.400
So what exactly are we making?

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.650
Sukiyaki!

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:28.940
Shabu Shabu.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.320
Mizutaki!

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:31.570
Vegetable pot.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.820
Seafood pot.

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.140
Late-night pot.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.910
No, um, wait...

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.740
Are we making all of those?

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:43.010
And there was a weird one at the end,

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:44.080
Miss Second in Command.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:49.570
Well, when we were trying to think
of what to make at the supermarket,

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:52.760
we just couldn't decide.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:56.130
So we decided to make it all.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:58.130
People call it "mystery pot."

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:00.630
So bring something you like.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:03.910
No, no. Hold on a second.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:08.590
We were supposed to make 
dinner together today.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.610
So when we thought about 
making a stew pot,

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:15.820
nobody said anything about 
making all this stuff.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:22.730
When you're going to eat something 
that's so bad for you,

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:25.330
you need to prepare 
your body and soul...

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:31.010
Or somebody weak like me 
will end up really regretting it.

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:35.790
So I'd rather not do that today.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:39.200
You just throw it in there?

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:41.730
Olive oil?

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.190
And then tofu within tofu.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:49.060
That was supposed to be 
another joke, wasn't it?

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:49.780
Yeah.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.310
Um, well...

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:55.600
If you could consider my condition...

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.810
Toshi, Souji's saying something.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.390
Then I'll put this in, too.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.160
A health supplement.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.970
Now you don't have to worry.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.350
That's not the issue!

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.810
Let's see, how about some butter?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:10.500
Souji's buttering us up. Get it?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.590
Not funny.

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.470
This looks like a mess.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.490
It's a really weird color.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:19.600
Can we actually eat this?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.080
It's fine.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:24.210
For now, we've only put in 
things you can eat, right?

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:27.040
Oh, Shi's got some Shi-take 
mushrooms right there.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.780
Now the meat.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.230
Kacchan, hand me that.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:31.620
Okay.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:32.690
Wait!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.750
That's beef!

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.940
And filet mignon!

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:38.640
Let's eat it normally...

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.180
Oh, Souji, stop interfering.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.330
Or you'll get filleted, too!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.900
I don't care, as long as you 
don't throw it in the pot!

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:47.580
Sorry!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:51.960
Now this!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.160
What's that?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.540
The guest of honor!

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.890
Then don't just throw it in a pot!

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.250
Let's go, Toshi!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.640
<b>The 

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:08.020
This can't be happening!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.480
How awful...

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:14.940
It's like one of those lakes of 
blood you see in pictures of hell.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.900
We can't eat this.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.850
It's fine.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:21.020
Don't worry.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:23.660
Why not?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.080
You ruined all those nice ingredients.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.870
Listen, you two.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:32.760
If you waste food, the 
food will laugh at you.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:36.010
And then every night, 
the souls of the food

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.790
will come to us to have their revenge.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:42.400
"Are there any bad girls here?" 
"Are there any bad girls here?"

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.970
They'll take your soul and...

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.700
We broke Souji.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.380
Snap out of it, Souji.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.280
Please don't hurt me.

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.320
Look at this.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:55.170
Curry?

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.550
The savior of meals that 
have lost their way.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:59.810
And who made them lose their way?

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:02.450
It will salvage our meal as well.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.410
That's right, curry is 
the god of pot dishes.

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.660
Okay, done!

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:11.450
Huh?

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:12.710
I'm surprised.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:13.790
It's not bad.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:15.240
Right?

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.070
The curry functions as a conductor

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.020
to bring out the nature of 
the different ingredients.

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:21.970
A splendid trick.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:26.510
You could even say this was 
the taste I wanted all along.

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:29.200
Then you were planning 
this the whole time?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:34.500
Only by pushing 
the limits of creativity

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.070
can new heights of invention be achieved.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:40.630
This applies to curry as well.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.850
Is that so?

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:45.080
We should've just 
started with curry, then.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.900
But that takes all the fun out of it.

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:50.050
There's plenty for seconds.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:52.770
No, I don't think I can eat that much.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.040
Toshi, ready for dessert?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.090
Yeah.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.090
<b>Strawberry 
Daifuku</b>

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.170
Strawberry Daifuku?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.220
I love these.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.550
Can I have one?

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.940
Just a second.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.130
It's not fun to just eat 
them like that, right?

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.810
They'll taste much better this way!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.860
You're going to pay

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:23.110
for doing something so horrible 
to my beloved Daifuku...

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:31.430
Apologize to my Strawberry Daifuku!

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.930
Though Okita Souji,
the White Lily, is sickly and weak,

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:40.980
she's said to be the 
strongest of them all...

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:46.100
And the nature of her 
strength is now revealed.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.510
I'm sorry.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.520
We won't do it anymore.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.830
<i>It's summer on a hot day.</i>

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:54.850
<i>No, it's hot on a summer day.</i>

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.850
<i>No, summer on a hot day.</i>

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:56.860
<i>No, summer is hot.</i>

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:03.300
Um, I've been saying 
this for a while now...

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:07.810
I have a test tomorrow, 
so I can't talk to you now.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.830
And I hate to ask this,

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.450
but are you ready for your own tests?

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.490
Are we?

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:16.710
I don't know.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:20.840
If you get held back again this year...

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:24.220
You won't be my upperclassmen anymore.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.100
What are you talking about?

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:33.220
We'll always be your 
upperclassmen in your heart.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.070
Well...

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:37.490
Anyway, that's enough studying.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.380
Why not take a break?

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:41.230
Okay? Stawberry Daifuku?

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.630
Do you have some Stawberry Daifuku?

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:46.480
I was just in the mood for some.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.440
That again?

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:50.770
Come on, don't be stingy.

00:21:50.770 --> 00:21:51.540
Stingy?

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:54.520
You never paid me back for last time!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:56.130
Don't be such a miser.

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.480
Who's a miser?

00:21:58.480 --> 00:22:01.110
This is Hinomoto Girls Academy.

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:03.730
A girls' boarding high school.

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:07.590
And here, in the Shinsen Dorm live beautiful girls also known as:

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:13.590
Golden Peony, Black 
Bellfower, and White Lily.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:50.170
Next time is the Annihilator 
Princess, Mogami Yoshiaki-chan!

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:53.850
Next time on Sengoku Collection: 
"Annihilator Princess."

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:56.460
Anybody who screws up and 
calls her Yoshimitsu

00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:59.020
is going to have to commit seppuku!
